---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title={"An Arc Browser Alternative for Mac, Windows and Linux | Blanc"}
  description={"Moving on from Arc? Blanc is a free, minimal Chromium browser that can bring your Arc Spaces over, with tab groups, vertical tabs and built-in ad blocking."}
  path="/arc-alternative"
  page="arc-alternative"
  current="features"
  ogDescription={"What Blanc offers if you are looking at what to use after Arc, and what it does not do."}
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline slot="head">
{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://blanc.day/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Arc alternative","item":"https://blanc.day/arc-alternative"}]}
</script>

<main id="main-content" class="feature-page feature-detail-page">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">arc alternative</span></nav>
  <section class="feature-hero feature-hero--detail feature-hero--text" aria-labelledby="arc-title">
    <h1 id="arc-title">Looking for an Arc alternative? Here is what Blanc does.</h1>
    <p>Bring the Arc Spaces you choose into Blanc as separate spaces, with pinned tabs, Today tabs and folders converted to tab groups. The guide below explains what transfers, what stays in Arc and how to start the import.</p>
    <p>This is a tab import, not a transfer of your accounts or browsing history. Blanc reads Arc’s sidebar file without changing it.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--top" aria-labelledby="arc-before-title">
    <div><h2 id="arc-before-title">Before you switch</h2></div>
    <div class="arc-transfer">
      <table aria-labelledby="arc-before-title">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">From Arc</th><th scope="col">In Blanc</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Selected Spaces</th><td>Separate Blanc Spaces</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Pinned tabs and Today tabs</th><td>Tabs in the imported space; loose pinned tabs remain pinned</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Folders</th><td>Tab groups</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Top-row Favorites, if selected</th><td>A Favorites folder named Arc</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Sign-ins, passwords, history and archived tabs</th><td>Not imported</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Notes and Easels</th><td>Not imported</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Blanc does not install extensions from the Chrome Web Store or include an AI assistant. If either is essential to you, check those limits before switching. Importing your tabs does not sign you into their websites.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="arc-move-title">
    <div><h2 id="arc-move-title">How to bring your Arc Spaces into Blanc</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>1. Open Bring Your Tabs.</h3><p>In Blanc, press ⌘L on Mac or Ctrl+L on Windows and Linux, then run <code>/bring-tabs</code>.</p></article>
      <article><h3>2. Choose your Arc data.</h3><p>Use the Arc option to preview your Spaces. If Blanc cannot find the sidebar file, use Choose file… to select <code>StorableSidebar.json</code>. On Linux, select a copy of that file from your Mac or Windows computer.</p></article>
      <article><h3>3. Review and import.</h3><p>Select the Spaces you want and decide whether to include Arc’s top-row Favorites, then confirm the import. Each selected Space becomes a <a href="/features/workspaces">Blanc Space</a>. Open an imported space when you are ready to use it.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="arc-carry-title">
    <div><h2 id="arc-carry-title">A calm browser built around one small island.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>Tabs down the side, if you want them.</h3><p>Switch on <a href="/features/vertical-tabs">optional vertical tabs</a> for a persistent, resizable tab list. The island stays your address bar and command surface.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Sets of tabs for different work.</h3><p><a href="/features/tab-groups">Named tab groups</a> keep related tabs together and fold away when you want a quieter view. <a href="/features/workspaces">Blanc Spaces</a>, free for everyone, save a window’s tabs and groups so you can switch between sets in place.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Two pages at once.</h3><p><a href="/features/glance">Glance</a> opens another tab as a card over the page you are using. Move or resize it, open it as a tab, or keep the two side by side in Split View.</p></article>
      <article><h3>One shortcut for everything.</h3><p>Press ⌘L on a Mac or Ctrl+L on Windows and Linux to <a href="/features/command-palette">search the web, switch tabs, find history and favorites, or run slash commands</a>.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Separate profiles.</h3><p><a href="/features/profiles">Local profiles</a> separate cookies, site data, Favorites, history and permissions, with no account required.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Ads blocked from the first launch.</h3><p><a href="/features/ad-blocking">Blanc Blocker</a> is on by default. On supported builds you can choose full uBlock Origin for regular tabs instead.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Bookmarks from other browsers.</h3><p>Blanc can import bookmarks into Favorites from Chromium-based browsers installed on your computer, such as Chrome, Edge and Brave.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Free, and open source.</h3><p>Blanc is free for macOS, Windows and Linux. Blanc’s own code is MIT-licensed and public on GitHub; its name, logos and third-party components keep their own terms.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-close" aria-labelledby="arc-close-title"><h2 id="arc-close-title">Ready to bring your Arc Spaces into Blanc?</h2><a class="cta" href="/download" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="arc-alternative" data-cta-position="feature-close">download blanc</a></section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .arc-transfer { min-width: 0; }
  .arc-transfer table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; table-layout: fixed; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .arc-transfer th, .arc-transfer td { padding: 16px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--site-border); text-align: left; vertical-align: top; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .arc-transfer th { font-weight: 600; }
  .arc-transfer thead th { border-top: 1px solid var(--site-border); }
  .arc-transfer td, .arc-transfer > p { color: var(--site-text-dim); }
  .arc-transfer > p { margin: 24px 0 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .arc-transfer th, .arc-transfer td { padding: 12px 8px; }
  }
</style>
